<%
# Cluster notice: read the overlay file directly. vulcan-status just cats this
# same file (/etc/vulcan-motd/announce.txt) with an ANSI-yellow "» Notice"
# header; the OOD MOTD used --plain (no colour), which is why it showed no
# yellow here. Reading the file directly avoids shelling out on every page
# render, and the alert box below restores the yellow the SSH banner has.
notice =
  begin
    File.read('/etc/vulcan-motd/announce.txt').to_s.strip
  rescue StandardError
    ""
  end
%>
* **Support:** [support@tech.alliancecan.ca](mailto:support@tech.alliancecan.ca)
* **Documentation:** [Vulcan Wiki](https://docs.alliancecan.ca/wiki/Vulcan) · [Getting Started](https://docs.alliancecan.ca/wiki/Getting_started) · [Running Jobs](https://docs.alliancecan.ca/wiki/Running_jobs) · [AMII Engineering Docs](https://docs.engineering.amii.ca)
* **Portals:** [Alliance CCDB Portal](https://ccdb.alliancecan.ca/) · [Vulcan Metrix Portal](https://portal.vulcan.alliancecan.ca/) · [Globus Portal](https://app.globus.org)
* **AI Tools:** [Aleph Inference Service](https://inference.vulcan.alliancecan.ca) · [Vulcan Open WebUI](https://llm.vulcan.alliancecan.ca/) · [Vulcan RagFlow](https://ragflow.vulcan.alliancecan.ca/)
* **Partners:** [Alberta Machine Intelligence Institute (AMII)](https://www.amii.ca/) · [Digital Research Alliance of Canada](https://alliancecan.ca/)
<% unless notice.empty? %>
<div class="alert alert-warning mb-2" role="alert">
<strong>Notice:</strong> <%= notice %>
</div>
<% end %>
